# Signs cookies and derives verification/state tokens; generate a long random value (e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`) and set it on the Convex deployment with `npx convex env set`, never commit the real value. The placeholder below is deliberately short and obviously fake — it fails createAuth's own guard (must be present, must not be Better Auth's public default, must be at least 32 characters) if pasted in verbatim.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=CHANGE-ME-not-a-real-secret

# Public origin of the site that owns the Better Auth session (e.g. https://admin.illith.com in production); set on the Convex deployment with `npx convex env set`.
SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Both variables are only required for auth instances that serve HTTP requests
# (convex/http.ts's createAuth call, which runs on the app deployment where these
# are set). Regenerating the Better Auth schema does NOT require either variable:
# convex/betterAuth/auth.ts is an introspection-only shim for the schema generator
# — it is never reachable as a Convex function and never serves a request — and it
# explicitly opts out with `createAuth({} as any, { requireSecret: false })`. That
# is the only place in the codebase allowed to do so (`grep -rn "requireSecret:
# false" packages/backend` must return exactly that one line); every other call
# goes through the default, which throws rather than letting better-auth fall back
# to its publicly-known default secret.
